# An allowlist, not a denylist: the Dockerfile copies the build context, and a
# checkout holds things that must never reach an image - `.env` (broker credentials),
# the gitignored `specs/`, `configs/` and `logs/` (a campaign's private strategy
# evidence and journal), `cache/`, `.git`, virtual environments and node_modules.
# A denylist misses the next one somebody adds; this names only what the image runs.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!main.py
!tradeflow/
!example/

# Even inside the allowed trees.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.venv
